// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO47-54 - dedicated onboard ESP32-C6 WiFi
// companion SDIO pins (see vendor pins_arduino.h BOARD_SDIO_* lines).
// pfodWeb NOTE: GPIO44 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard
// addressable RGB LED. Vendor pins_arduino.h defines
// #define PIN_RGB_LED 44 and encodes LED_BUILTIN/RGB_BUILTIN as a
// virtual pin (SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT + PIN_RGB_LED) for the new
// rgbLedWrite() API - same encoding pattern as Unexpected Maker boards
// (RGB_BUILTIN = RGB_DATA + SOC_GPIO_PIN_COUNT); real GPIO is 44, not
// an offset pin number. No BOOT/user pushbutton tagged - pins_arduino.h
// only has boilerplate "// BOOT_MODE 35 / // BOOT_MODE2 36 pullup"
// comments (no #define, identical text copied across all esp32p4
// variants incl. generic esp32p4 and m5stack_tab5) with no vendor
// source confirming a physical button on this specific board - see
// notes.txt for research trail.
